WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:03.549 --> 00:00:09.539
In the first part we saw that Force is not just a human pushing or pulling an object.

00:00:10.150 --> 00:00:12.300
Force is a push or pull upon an object

00:00:12.910 --> 00:00:15.359
resulting from its interaction with another object.

00:00:16.420 --> 00:00:18.569
There are two things we will cover in this video :

00:00:19.359 --> 00:00:22.319
Types of forces and the effects of forces

00:00:23.050 --> 00:00:26.730
For simplicity we can classify forces into two types

00:00:27.430 --> 00:00:29.849
Contact forces and Non-contact forces.

00:00:31.029 --> 00:00:33.029
Contact forces are just what they sound like

00:00:33.760 --> 00:00:38.736
Forces that result from the interaction of two objects in contact with each other.

00:00:38.736 --> 00:00:40.920
Are there any contact forces that you know of?

00:00:41.649 --> 00:00:43.270
Of course you know a few!

00:00:43.270 --> 00:00:46.409
What happens when you softly kick the ball which is lying on the ground?

00:00:47.110 --> 00:00:50.399
You apply the force on the ball, and there was contact.

00:00:51.250 --> 00:00:53.789
Applied Force is one of the contact forces.

00:00:54.969 --> 00:00:58.649
Next there is a force of friction which brings the ball to a halt.

00:00:58.989 --> 00:01:03.899
As the ball is in contact with the ground,  frictional force is also a contact force.

00:01:04.839 --> 00:01:06.839
Don't you think there was some air resistance?

00:01:07.570 --> 00:01:08.890
Yes!

00:01:08.890 --> 00:01:11.182
Air resistance too is a contact force.

00:01:11.182 --> 00:01:16.470
The normal force which is applied force in the upward direction is a contact force as well

00:01:17.439 --> 00:01:21.869
These were some of the contact forces we know of but these are not the only ones.

00:01:22.810 --> 00:01:25.440
Can you think of any non-contact force?

00:01:25.440 --> 00:01:27.732
What happens when the ball is in the air?

00:01:27.732 --> 00:01:29.129
It will fall down, right?

00:01:29.680 --> 00:01:31.240
What pulls the ball down?

00:01:31.240 --> 00:01:36.329
Yes, it's the gravitational pull which is trying to pull the ball towards the center of the earth.

00:01:37.240 --> 00:01:41.460
This pull happens even if the object is not in physical contact with the earth.

00:01:41.950 --> 00:01:46.320
The gravitational force is an example of a non-contact force.

00:01:47.439 --> 00:01:51.359
Other examples of non-contact forces are electrical and magnetic forces.

00:01:53.110 --> 00:01:56.400
Now i want you to think about the next question i'm going to ask you.

00:01:57.190 --> 00:01:59.190
What all can a force do?

00:01:59.350 --> 00:02:01.350
What can be its effects?

00:02:01.450 --> 00:02:02.880
Let me give an example.

00:02:02.880 --> 00:02:05.850
Force can set a stationary object in motion.

00:02:06.610 --> 00:02:08.600
That's one of the things force can do.

00:02:08.600 --> 00:02:11.160
Can you think of the other things it can do?

00:02:14.950 --> 00:02:19.440
Assume an object is moving at a uniform velocity of two meters per second.

00:02:19.440 --> 00:02:22.470
If it is pushed harder its velocity will increase.

00:02:23.380 --> 00:02:26.740
So force can also change the velocity of an object.

00:02:26.740 --> 00:02:29.490
Force can also stop a moving object.

00:02:30.640 --> 00:02:32.640
Anything else you can think of?

00:02:32.950 --> 00:02:36.880
Yes, force can also change the direction of a moving object.

00:02:36.880 --> 00:02:39.429
If a ball is moving towards the north,

00:02:39.429 --> 00:02:43.139
a kid from the right can change its direction to north-west.

00:02:43.840 --> 00:02:46.460
Is there anything else you can think of force can do?

00:02:46.460 --> 00:02:48.990
Come on! I want you to think really hard.

00:02:49.930 --> 00:02:52.140
Don't think only in terms of motion.

00:02:54.970 --> 00:02:57.460
Force can also change the shape of an object.

00:02:57.460 --> 00:03:02.669
If we apply force from both sides to a spherical ball, its shape changes.

00:03:03.130 --> 00:03:06.329
The ball's position does not change, but its shape does.

00:03:07.060 --> 00:03:09.929
So these are some of the things that force can do.

00:03:10.660 --> 00:03:17.010
In the next video we will play an interesting game to know if you really understood how forces act on an object.

